    "goal": "Extrude bioink through a UV-4 (200 µm) nozzle along a 35239 µm G-code path at 18.22 mm/min, filling a 2687 µm-wide footprint at 192 µm line pitch, and report extruded ink volume and fill-line count.",
    "rationale": "Bioprinting extrusion design. The extruded ink volume is computed from the nozzle diameter (200 µm) and the G-code path length (35239 µm) as a cylindrical filament: V = π(d/2)²·L. The number of fill lines is the footprint width (2687 µm) divided by the centre-to-centre line pitch (192 µm), rounded up. Ink density (1.086 g/cm³) is provided for filament-mass context. These are the raw inputs; all derived values (extrusion volume, print time, extrusion rate, filament mass, lines to cover) are computed and verified by the system.",
